From: meta-sharebox maintainers <leo@magacyber.fr>
Subject: [PATCH] Serve uploads on the main listener and allow a separate listing folder

ShareBox only opens TCP port 80 on the access point, so the droopy
compatible upload server on port 8080 is unreachable from clients.

- Mount the upload form on the main listener under /upload/ when
  DROOPY_ENABLED is "yes", and make the start page iframe point there.
- DROOPY_PORT="0" disables the separate upload listener.
- Use relative links and redirects in the upload pages so they work under
  a path prefix as well as on their own port.
- New DIRLIST_FOLDER key (default: UPLOADFOLDER) selects the folder listed
  under /Shared, so the whole public share can be browsed while uploads
  land in a dedicated subfolder.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: meta-sharebox maintainers <leo@magacyber.fr>
---
--- a/assets/www_content/index.html
+++ b/assets/www_content/index.html
@@ -44,8 +44,8 @@
 		<div id="sidebar">
 			<div id="upload" class="card">
 				<h2 data-l10n-id="sidebarUpload">Upload</h2>
-				<iframe width="100%" height="80" src='http://luffy.lan:8080' data-l10n-id="sidebarIframeNotSupported" scrolling="no">
-					Your browser does not support iframes.. If you want to upload something, follow this <a href='http://luffy.lan:8080' data-l10n-id="link">Link</a>.
+				<iframe width="100%" height="80" src='/upload/' data-l10n-id="sidebarIframeNotSupported" scrolling="no">
+					Your browser does not support iframes.. If you want to upload something, follow this <a href='/upload/' data-l10n-id="link">Link</a>.
 				</iframe>
 				<h3><a href="/Shared" data-l10n-id="sidebarBrowseFiles">Browse Files -></a></h3>
 			<div id="station"></div>
